  "summary": "This <b>classic Greek fasolada</b> is a rich, comforting white bean soup deeply rooted in traditional Mediterranean home cooking. Built around tender navy beans, chopped sweet carrots, crisp celery, and sweet yellow onions, this vibrant dish receives a luscious boost from generous amounts of extra virgin olive oil added toward the end of cooking. Designed specifically as a <b>convenient make-ahead meal</b>, the aromatic vegetable broth and creamy white beans continue to absorb flavor while chilling in the refrigerator overnight. Reheating gentle simmered broth actually deepens the savory garlic and tomato background notes, producing a thicker and more harmonious texture on the second day. Fresh oregano and a bright finish of squeezed lemon juice balance the hearty beans, making this colorful soup satisfying yet surprisingly light. Pair this wholesome soup with crusty sourdough bread, salty feta cheese, and kalamata olives for a complete rustic tavern experience right at your home dining table.",
